<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="auth-service-guide" xml:lang="en-us">
  <title id="topic-title">Authentication Service Configuration</title>
  <shortdesc id="shortdesc">This topic describes how to configure the Authentication Service, the
    supported feature flags, and the REST endpoints that the service exposes.</shortdesc>
  <body>
    <section id="sec-overview">
      <title id="title-overview">Overview</title>
      <?oxy_comment_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T101500+0300" comment="Reworded the first sentence. Please confirm the wording with the Identity team." id="cmt-p-intro"?><p
        id="p-intro" outputclass="lead">The Authentication Service verifies the user credentials and
        issues signed access tokens. It runs as a stateless component and can be scaled
        horizontally<?oxy_delete author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T102000+0300" content=" behind a load
        balancer"?>.</p><?oxy_comment_end?>
      <p id="p-arch">Tokens are signed with the key configured in
        <codeph>auth.signing.key</codeph>. <?oxy_comment_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T101700+0300" comment="Is this still true for deployments that use sticky sessions?" id="cmt-p-arch-sel"?>The
        service keeps no session state at all, so any instance can serve any request without a
        sticky session.<?oxy_comment_end?></p>
      <note id="note-warn" type="warning"><?oxy_comment_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T101800+0300" comment="Also mention the secret store here." id="cmt-note-warn" flag="done"?>Never
        commit the signing key to source control.<?oxy_comment_end?></note>
    </section>
    <section id="sec-config">
      <title id="title-config"><?oxy_comment_start author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T103000+0300" comment="Rename this section to 'Service configuration' for consistency with the other topics." id="cmt-title-config"?>Configuring
        the service<?oxy_comment_end?></title>
      <p id="p-config-lead">The configuration file is read once, at startup.
          <?oxy_comment_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T103100+0300" comment="First of two adjacent comments: describe the rolling restart procedure." id="cmt-cfg-1"?>Restart
        the service after every change.<?oxy_comment_end?>
          <?oxy_comment_start author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T103200+0300" comment="Second of two adjacent comments: link to the hot reload feature request." id="cmt-cfg-2"?>A
        hot reload of the configuration is not supported.<?oxy_comment_end?></p>
      <ul id="ul-prereq">
        <li id="li-prereq-1"><?oxy_comment_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T103300+0300" comment="Do we still support a JDK 17 runtime here?" id="cmt-li-prereq-1"?><?oxy_comment_start author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T103400+0300" comment="No, JDK 17 was dropped in release 4.2, so nothing to change." parentID="cmt-li-prereq-1" mid="1"?>A
          JDK 21 runtime is installed on the host.<?oxy_comment_end mid="1"?><?oxy_comment_end?></li>
        <li id="li-prereq-2">The database schema is migrated to revision 47.</li>
        <li id="li-prereq-4">A signing key of at least
            <?oxy_delete author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T103500+0300" content="256"?><?oxy_insert_start author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T103500+0300"?>384<?oxy_insert_end?>
          bits is available.</li>
        <li id="li-prereq-5">The audit collector endpoint is reachable from the host.</li>
      </ul>
      <ol id="ol-steps">
        <li id="li-step-1">Stop the running service
          instance<?oxy_insert_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T103600+0300"?> and wait
          for the open connections to drain<?oxy_insert_end?>.</li>
        <li id="li-step-2"><?oxy_comment_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T103700+0300" comment="Add the full path of the file for Windows installations." id="cmt-li-step-2"?>Edit
            <filepath>conf/auth-service.properties</filepath> and set the signing
          key.<?oxy_comment_end?></li>
        <li id="li-step-4">Start the service and check the health endpoint.</li>
        <li id="li-step-3">Validate the configuration with <codeph>authctl verify</codeph>.</li>
      </ol>
      <?oxy_comment_start author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T103800+0300" comment="Add the auth.audit.target property to this example." id="cmt-cb-config"?><codeblock
        id="cb-config" outputclass="language-properties">auth.signing.key=file:/etc/auth/signing.pem
auth.token.ttl=7200
auth.audit.enabled=true
auth.audit.target=collector:9000</codeblock><?oxy_comment_end?>
    </section>
    <section id="sec-migration">
      <title id="title-migration">Migrating from release 4.1</title>
      <p id="p-migration-lead">Release 4.2 changes the default token lifetime and removes the
        in-process session cache. Plan the following steps before the upgrade.</p>
      <ul id="ul-migration">
        <li id="li-migration-1">Export the active sessions with <codeph>authctl dump-sessions</codeph>.</li>
        <li id="li-migration-2">Increase the connection pool of the user store by 50 percent.</li>
        <li id="li-migration-3">Re-issue the tokens that were signed with a 256 bit key.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section id="sec-features">
      <title id="title-features">Feature flags</title>
      <?oxy_delete author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T104000+0300" content="&lt;p id=&quot;p-features-lead&quot;&gt;The following flags control the modules that are loaded at startup.&lt;/p&gt;"?>
      <table id="table-features" frame="topbot" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
        <title id="title-table-features">Supported feature flags</title>
        <tgroup cols="4">
          <colspec colname="c1" colnum="1" colwidth="1.2*"/>
          <colspec colname="c2" colnum="2" colwidth="3*"/>
          <colspec colname="c3" colnum="3" colwidth="1*"/>
          <colspec colname="c4" colnum="4" colwidth="1.2*"/>
          <thead>
            <row id="row-features-head">
              <entry id="e-h-feature">Feature</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-desc">Description</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-status">Status</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-owner">Owner</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row id="row-auth">
              <entry id="e-auth-name">Authentication</entry>
              <entry id="e-auth-desc">Validates the user credentials against the configured user
                store and issues a signed access token that is valid for
                  <?oxy_comment_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T104100+0300" comment="Comment on a text fragment inside a table cell: keep this value in sync with the Limits table." id="cmt-e-auth-desc-text"?>two
                hours<?oxy_comment_end?>. Both password based, certificate based and SSO logins are
                supported.</entry>
              <entry id="e-auth-status">Active</entry>
              <entry id="e-auth-owner">Identity team</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-authz">
              <entry id="e-authz-name">Authorization</entry>
              <entry id="e-authz-desc">Evaluates the role and group assignments of the authenticated
                user and returns the effective permission set for the requested resource, including
                the permissions inherited from the parent groups.</entry>
              <?oxy_comment_start author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T104200+0300" comment="Comment on a table cell: is this module really still fully active?" id="cmt-e-authz-status"?><entry
                id="e-authz-status">Active</entry><?oxy_comment_end?>
              <entry id="e-authz-owner">Platform team</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-log" rowsep="0">
              <?oxy_comment_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T104300+0300" comment="Comment on a whole table row: this row must be reviewed by the Observability team before release." id="cmt-row-log"?>
              <entry id="e-log-name">Logging</entry>
              <entry id="e-log-desc">Writes one structured audit record for every authentication
                attempt, including the client address and the outcome of the attempt.</entry>
              <entry id="e-log-status">Planned</entry>
              <entry id="e-log-owner">Observability team</entry><?oxy_comment_end?>
            </row>
            <row id="row-sec">
              <entry id="e-sec-name">Security</entry>
              <entry id="e-sec-desc">Applies the hardening profile: strict transport security,
                request rate
                limiting,<?oxy_insert_start author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T104400+0300"?>
                mandatory TLS 1.3,<?oxy_insert_end?> and rejection of weak cipher suites.</entry>
              <entry id="e-sec-status" align="center">Testing</entry>
              <entry id="e-sec-owner">Security team</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-metrics">
              <entry id="e-metrics-name">Metrics</entry>
              <entry id="e-metrics-desc">Exposes the token issuing counters and the latency
                histograms on the <filepath>/metrics</filepath> endpoint.</entry>
              <entry id="e-metrics-status">Planned</entry>
              <entry id="e-metrics-owner">Observability team</entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section id="sec-endpoints">
      <title id="title-endpoints">REST endpoints</title>
      <p id="p-endpoints-lead">All endpoints are relative to the service context path and require a
        JSON request body.</p>
      <table id="table-endpoints" frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
        <title id="title-table-endpoints">Endpoints of the authentication API</title>
        <tgroup cols="4">
          <colspec colname="m1" colnum="1" colwidth="1*"/>
          <colspec colname="m2" colnum="2" colwidth="1.6*"/>
          <colspec colname="m3" colnum="3" colwidth="3*"/>
          <colspec colname="m4" colnum="4" colwidth="0.8*"/>
          <thead>
            <row id="row-ep-head">
              <entry id="e-h-method">Method</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-path">Path</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-epdesc">Description</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-since">Since</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row id="row-ep-login">
              <entry id="e-login-method"><codeph>POST</codeph></entry>
              <entry id="e-login-path"><filepath>/auth/login</filepath></entry>
              <entry id="e-login-desc">Exchanges the credentials sent in the
                <parmname>username</parmname> and <parmname>password</parmname> fields for an access
                token. Returns <codeph>401</codeph> when the credentials are rejected.</entry>
              <entry id="e-login-since">4.0</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-ep-refresh">
              <entry id="e-refresh-method"><codeph>POST</codeph></entry>
              <entry id="e-refresh-path"><filepath>/auth/refresh</filepath></entry>
              <entry id="e-refresh-desc">Issues a new access token for a still valid
                <parmname>refreshToken</parmname>. The old token is invalidated as described in
                <xref href="#auth-service-guide/sec-limits" format="dita">Limits</xref>.</entry>
              <entry id="e-refresh-since">4.0</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-ep-logout">
              <entry id="e-logout-method"><codeph>POST</codeph></entry>
              <entry id="e-logout-path"><filepath>/auth/logout</filepath></entry>
              <entry id="e-logout-desc">Invalidates the current access token. The client should also
                clear the token from its local storage.</entry>
              <entry id="e-logout-since">4.0</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-ep-keys">
              <entry id="e-keys-method"><codeph>GET</codeph></entry>
              <entry id="e-keys-path"><filepath>/auth/keys</filepath></entry>
              <entry id="e-keys-desc">Returns the public part of the signing key so that downstream
                services can verify the tokens without calling the service.</entry>
              <entry id="e-keys-since">4.2</entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section id="sec-limits">
      <title id="title-limits">Limits</title>
      <table id="table-limits" frame="topbot" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
        <?oxy_attributes colsep="&lt;change type=&quot;modified&quot; oldValue=&quot;0&quot; author=&quot;Ana Popescu&quot; timestamp=&quot;20260903T104500+0300&quot; /&gt;"?>
        <title id="title-table-limits">Runtime limits</title>
        <tgroup cols="4">
          <colspec colname="l1" colnum="1" colwidth="1.4*"/>
          <colspec colname="l2" colnum="2" colwidth="1*"/>
          <colspec colname="l3" colnum="3" colwidth="1*"/>
          <colspec colname="l4" colnum="4" colwidth="2.6*"/>
          <thead>
            <row id="row-lim-head">
              <entry id="e-h-param">Parameter</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-default">Default</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-max">Maximum</entry>
              <entry id="e-h-notes">Notes</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row id="row-lim-ttl">
              <entry id="e-lim-ttl-name">Token lifetime</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-ttl-def">3600</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-ttl-max">86400</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-ttl-notes">Expressed in seconds. Longer lifetimes increase the window
                in which a leaked token can be replayed.</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-lim-rate">
              <entry id="e-lim-rate-name">Requests per minute</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-rate-def">600</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-rate-max">6000</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-rate-notes">Counted per client address. Requests over the limit are
                answered with <codeph>429</codeph>.</entry>
            </row>
            <row id="row-lim-pool">
              <entry id="e-lim-pool-name">Connection pool size</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-pool-def">20</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-pool-max">200</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-pool-notes">Applies to the connection pool of the user store.</entry>
            </row>
            <?oxy_insert_start author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T104600+0300"?>
            <row id="row-lim-clock">
              <entry id="e-lim-clock-name">Clock skew</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-clock-def">30</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-clock-max">300</entry>
              <entry id="e-lim-clock-notes">Tolerated difference, in seconds, between the clock of
                the token issuer and the clock of the verifier.</entry>
            </row>
            <?oxy_insert_end?>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section id="sec-deploy">
      <title id="title-deploy">Deployment profiles</title>
      <p id="p-deploy-lead">Three deployment profiles are supported out of the
        box<?oxy_insert_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T104700+0300"?>, and a custom
        profile can be derived from any of them<?oxy_insert_end?>.</p>
      <ul id="ul-profiles">
        <li id="li-profile-dev">Development
          <ol id="ol-dev-details">
            <li id="li-dev-1">A single instance with an in-memory user store.</li>
            <li id="li-dev-2">Audit logging is disabled.</li>
          </ol>
        </li>
        <li id="li-profile-stage">Staging
          <ul id="ul-stage-details">
            <li id="li-stage-1">Two instances behind a load balancer.</li>
            <li id="li-stage-2">A shared PostgreSQL user store.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li id="li-profile-prod">Production
          <ul id="ul-prod-details">
            <li id="li-prod-1">At least three
              instances<?oxy_delete author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T104800+0300" content=", in separate availability zones"?>.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li id="li-prod-2">Audit records are shipped to the central collector.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section id="sec-trouble">
      <title id="title-trouble">Troubleshooting</title>
      <dl id="dl-trouble">
        <dlentry id="dlentry-401">
          <dt id="dt-401">Every request is answered with 401</dt>
          <dd id="dd-401">The signing key is not the same on all instances. Redeploy the shared key
            and restart the instances one by one.</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry id="dlentry-slow">
          <dt id="dt-slow-tokens">Token issuing is slow</dt>
          <dd id="dd-slow">The user store is almost always the bottleneck. Check the size of the
            connection pool, the latency of the store, and the number of queued requests that is
            reported on the metrics endpoint.</dd>
        </dlentry>
      </dl>
      <?oxy_insert_start author="Ana Popescu" timestamp="20260903T104900+0300"?>
      <p id="p-trouble-metrics">Before you open a ticket, capture the output of the
          <filepath>/metrics</filepath> endpoint for a full minute.</p>
      <?oxy_insert_end?>
      <?oxy_comment_start author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T105000+0300" comment="This comment covers a region that also contains a tracked insertion." id="cmt-p-trouble-end"?><p
        id="p-trouble-end">If the problem persists, open a support ticket for the Identity
        team<?oxy_insert_start author="Dan Ionescu" timestamp="20260903T105100+0300"?> and attach the
        correlation id of a failed request<?oxy_insert_end?>.</p><?oxy_comment_end?>
      <p id="p-legacy">The legacy <apiname>SessionManager</apiname> component is still shipped for
        backward compatibility and will be removed in the next major release.</p>
    </section>
  </body>
</topic>
